# Git push policy

## Feature branch (default while iterating)

After a **meaningful chunk** of work on the current non-`main` branch:

1. **Commit** on that branch (clear message; no secrets).
2. **Push that branch only** (`git push -u origin HEAD`) so remote WIP stays current.

Do this without waiting for an explicit “push” / “commit” each time — keeps later merge-to-main easy.

If the user says “don’t push until I say” / “save only”, pause proactive push until they lift it.

## Main (hard gate)

- **Never** merge into `main`, `git push origin main`, or create a main-bound release unless the user clearly asks (e.g. “merge to main”, “push to main”).
- When they say “push” without naming main → push **only** the current feature branch.
